  <div>
    {% set heading = "FAQ" %}{% set desc = "" %}
    {% include "section-heading.njk" %}

    <div class="stack" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <details class="faq"><summary>What is filtered?</summary><p>Filtered mode blocks known risky destinations and known malicious infrastructure from curated AEGIS-DNS sources. Filtering is best-effort and may produce false positives or false negatives.</p></details>
      <details class="faq"><summary>What is not filtered?</summary><p>Open mode is intended for compatibility checks and behavior comparison. Managed policies may differ by customer scope. AEGIS PDNS is not a replacement for endpoint protection, browser security, patching, or user training.</p></details>
      <details class="faq"><summary>Can I test it before setup?</summary><p>Yes. Use the DNS test page to test selected resolver endpoints and the public canary domains.</p></details>
      <details class="faq"><summary>Can organizations request managed deployment?</summary><p>Yes. Contact SecretChip for beta access, managed deployment, commercial support, policy design, and operational rollout planning.</p></details>
      <details class="faq"><summary>Can I validate DoT and DoQ in the browser?</summary><p>No. Standard browser JavaScript cannot directly open raw TCP/853 for DoT or UDP/QUIC/853 for DoQ. The browser test focuses on DoH and public HTTPS canary checks.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>

